  "content": {
    "id": "p58-q29-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "29",
    "prompt": "Let $f(\\theta)=5-7\\cos\\theta+\\cos2\\theta+\\cos3\\theta$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p58-q29-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By using identities for $\\cos2\\theta$ and $\\cos3\\theta$, show that\n$$f(\\theta)=4\\cos^3\\theta+2\\cos^2\\theta-10\\cos\\theta+4.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f(\\theta)=4\\cos^3\\theta+2\\cos^2\\theta-10\\cos\\theta+4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(\\theta)&=5-7\\cos\\theta+(2\\cos^2\\theta-1)+(4\\cos^3\\theta-3\\cos\\theta)\\\\f(\\theta)&=4\\cos^3\\theta+2\\cos^2\\theta-10\\cos\\theta+4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p58-q29-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, solve $5-7\\cos\\theta+\\cos2\\theta+\\cos3\\theta=0$ for $0\\le\\theta\\le2\\pi$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0,\\ \\dfrac{\\pi}{3},\\ \\dfrac{5\\pi}{3},\\ 2\\pi$.\n\nSet $x=\\cos\\theta$ and factor the cubic; reject $x=-2$.",
          "worked": "Let $x=\\cos\\theta$. By part (a),\n$$4x^3+2x^2-10x+4=0.$$\nFor $P(x)=4x^3+2x^2-10x+4$, $P(1)=0$, so $x-1$ is a factor. Dividing and factorising gives\n$$\\begin{align*}4x^3+2x^2-10x+4&=2(x-1)(2x^2+3x-2)\\\\4x^3+2x^2-10x+4&=2(x-1)(2x-1)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=1,\\dfrac12,-2$. Since $-1\\le\\cos\\theta\\le1$, reject $x=-2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=1\\text{ or }\\frac12\\\\\\theta&=0,\\ \\frac{\\pi}{3},\\ \\frac{5\\pi}{3},\\ 2\\pi\\qquad(0\\le\\theta\\le2\\pi).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 96
      }
    ]
  },
